# Platinum Marquise Engagement Ring ({{year}}): Why 95% Purity Costs $2,400 More

![Three marquise cut diamonds held in jeweller tweezers against a soft grey backdrop with text overlay reading Platinum Marquise Ring Why 95 Purity Costs 2400 as the DiamondCritics featured image for the platinum marquise engagement ring guide](/images/platinum-marquise-engagement-ring.jpg "Platinum Marquise Engagement Ring Why 95 Purity Costs 2400")

## TL;DR — Platinum Marquise Engagement Ring in One Scroll

**A platinum marquise engagement ring is a marquise-cut diamond mounted in a 95% pure platinum setting.** Platinum costs $300–$600 more upfront than an equivalent 14k white gold setting. Over 50 years of wear, platinum saves $500–$1,500 in rhodium replating costs. That makes the lifetime cost roughly equal — or cheaper. Three things drive the upfront gap: metal purity (95% vs 58%), metal density (platinum weighs 60% more than gold), and fabrication labour (harder metal = more bench time).

**The 4-tier platinum marquise price stack:**

- **Tier 1 — Classic Solitaires ($1,180–$1,635):** Four-prong, six-prong, petite, cable, and woven solitaire silhouettes. No side stones. Purest platinum expression of the marquise shape.
- **Tier 2 — Pavé Entry ($1,770–$2,200):** Petite pavé, French pavé (1/4 ct.), Diamond Pavé (JA), petite cathedral pavé. Shoulder stones start here.
- **Tier 3 — Premium Pavé + Vintage ($2,315–$3,250):** Hand-engraved micropavé, graduated pavé, cross prong surprise, scalloped pavé, milgrain lace, marquise-accent side stone. Full vintage detailing available.
- **Tier 4 — Designer + Halo ($3,655–$5,015+):** Riviera Pavé, French Pavé (1ct.), Blue Nile Studio Imperial Micropavé, escalating baguette, falling edge halo. Statement pieces with certified setting weights.

→ Entry pick: **[Classic Four Prong Solitaire in Platinum at $1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — market floor, timeless silhouette.
→ Six-prong classic: **[Classic Six-Prong Solitaire in Platinum at $1,355](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-six-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194157?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — extra tip protection.
→ Pavé sweet spot: **[Six-Prong Petite Pavé in Platinum at $1,895](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/six-prong-petite-pave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194944?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — pavé shoulders + six-prong tip protection.
→ Vintage pick: **[Milgrain Lace Pavé in Platinum at $3,250 (JA)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/milgrain-lace-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-315054?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — Edwardian milgrain + lifetime platinum.

**Priority:** Platinum is worth the upfront premium if you want no-maintenance white metal for 50+ years. White gold at 14k saves $300–$600 now but costs $500–$1,500 in rhodium plating over the ring's life. See the full [marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond) for shape fundamentals.

## Expert Summary

Platinum marquise engagement ring pricing in current certified market inventory starts at **$1,180** for the Classic Four Prong Solitaire in Platinum and runs to **$5,015+** for the Escalating Baguette Side Stone Diamond in Platinum. 40+ platinum settings across every style. Add a 1ct G-colour marquise centre and the complete ring sits at $1,930 for lab, $4,180+ for natural.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/)-certified diamond expert. Platinum is the metal I recommend if you want your ring to look exactly the same on your 25th anniversary as it did on your wedding day. No replating, no colour shift, no metal loss. In 15+ years of grading, I have examined thousands of rings at the 10-, 20-, and 30-year mark. Platinum rings patina to a satin finish rather than losing metal. White gold rings lose their rhodium plating and require replating to recover. The lifetime economics almost always favour platinum for anyone who plans to wear the ring for decades. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every related topic.

This guide covers the Platinum Purity Premium, the No-Replating Lifetime Guarantee, the Platinum Hardness Paradox, 1ct to 2.5ct pairing math, and the full platinum marquise inventory from $1,180 to $5,015+. All prices verified against live certified inventory. Pricing presented as independent market research.

