## Pros and Cons of Platinum Marquise Engagement Rings

**Pros:**
- **No rhodium replating ever** — permanent white metal colour.
- **95% pure metal** — most precious-metal-dense ring you can buy.
- **Hypoallergenic** — no nickel allergy risk unlike 14k white gold alloys.
- **Metal displacement scratching** — satin patina, no metal loss over decades.
- **Heavier, premium feel** — if you want a substantial ring, you'll prefer platinum's weight.
- **Heirloom-grade durability** — platinum rings survive 100+ year life spans intact.
- **Lifetime cost beats white gold** — by year 25, the replating math reverses the upfront gap.

**Cons:**
- **$300–$600 upfront premium** — the entry cost is higher vs 14k white gold.
- **Fewer setting options** — 40+ platinum marquise settings vs 60+ in white gold.
- **Develops satin patina** — some people prefer the mirror finish and dislike the natural patina that develops. Polish every few years restores mirror.
- **Heavier** — a few grams difference per ring, but detectable to some.

> **"The patina question is the one that trips most people up. They see scratches on a platinum ring and think something went wrong. Nothing went wrong — that satin finish is normal platinum behaviour. You polish it once and it's a mirror again. In 15 years of doing this, I have never seen a platinum ring structurally fail from daily wear. White gold? I've resized and replated dozens of them. The two metals age very differently, and the difference compounds over time."** — Farzana Hasan, GIA Diamond Expert

## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is a platinum marquise engagement ring?

A platinum marquise engagement ring is a marquise-cut diamond mounted in a 950 platinum setting — 95% pure platinum. The metal reads bright white, never needs replating, and is fully hypoallergenic. The shape is marquise (pointed oval) and the setting is the most durable white-metal option available.

### Why does platinum cost more than white gold?

Three reasons: **purity** (95% platinum vs 58.3% gold), **density** (platinum is heavier per cm³, so rings use more metal by weight), and **fabrication** (platinum has a higher melting point and requires more bench labour). The upfront premium averages $300–$600 per setting.

### Is platinum worth the extra cost over 14k white gold for a marquise ring?

**Yes, for lifetime wearers.** White gold needs rhodium replating every 5–10 years ($100–$200 per visit). Over 50 years, that adds $750–$1,500 in maintenance costs — exceeding the $300–$600 upfront platinum premium. If you plan to wear the ring for 20+ years, platinum wins on total cost. See the [white gold marquise guide](/white-gold-marquise-engagement-ring) for the detailed comparison.

### How much does a platinum marquise engagement ring cost?

**Setting-only: $1,180 to $5,015+.** The entry floor is the Classic Four Prong Solitaire in Platinum at $1,180. The designer ceiling is the Escalating Baguette in Platinum at $5,015. Add a 1ct G-colour lab marquise at ~$750 and the complete ring starts at $1,930.

### Does platinum need maintenance?

**Minimal maintenance.** Polish every 5–10 years ($150–$300) to restore the mirror finish if you prefer it. Unlike white gold, platinum needs no rhodium replating — ever. The satin patina it develops over years is a natural platinum characteristic, not damage.

### What colour grade should I use with platinum?

**G minimum. F sweet spot.** Platinum's bright white shows any warm tint clearly — the cool metal contrasts with warm-tinted stones. Avoid I–K in platinum. G or F reads crisp white. H is marginal — check for grey (not brown) undertones. See our [marquise diamond colour guide](/marquise-diamond-color-guide) for full details.

### Is platinum harder than white gold?

**No — platinum is softer.** But softer doesn't mean more damaged-looking. Platinum scratches by metal displacement (no metal loss). White gold scratches by metal loss. Over time, platinum retains its volume while white gold physically thins. Polish restores both to mirror. This is the Platinum Hardness Paradox.

### What is the cheapest platinum marquise setting?

The cheapest certified platinum marquise setting is **[$1,180 for the Classic Four Prong Solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**. The Ten Prong Solitaire at $1,200 and the Comfort Fit Bezel at $1,250 are the next cheapest options.

### Does platinum turn yellow?

**Never.** Platinum's white colour is the metal itself — there is no coating to wear off. White gold turns yellow when its rhodium plating wears away. Platinum stays white permanently. Polishing restores the surface shine but the colour never changes.

### Is platinum good for an active lifestyle?

**Yes — it's the best metal for active wearers.** Metal displacement means scratches don't permanently damage the ring. No replating maintenance. No yellow cast from plating wear. The satin patina that develops over heavy wear can be polished back to mirror at any point.

### Can I resize a platinum marquise ring?

**Yes.** Platinum resizes well, though it requires a specialist jeweller due to the high melting point. Sizing up or down by 1.5 sizes is routine. Cost is typically $50–$150. The [marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond) has sizing and fit notes.

### What purity is platinum engagement rings?

**950 platinum** — 95% pure platinum + 5% alloy (usually ruthenium or cobalt for workability). Some platinum pieces are 900 (90%) or 850 (85%) platinum. Always confirm the hallmark. 950 Pt is the standard for fine jewellery and certified retailers.

### Does platinum scratch more easily than gold?

**Technically yes, but visually no.** Platinum is softer on the Vickers hardness scale than work-hardened 14k white gold alloys. But platinum scratches by displacing metal (not losing it), so it develops a patina rather than thinning. White gold scratches by losing metal — it thins over years. Polishing restores both. Practically, platinum looks better after decades of wear.

### What is the platinum purity stamp on a ring?

Look for **950 Pt**, **Pt950**, or **PLAT** hallmarks. These indicate 95% platinum content. Some older or import pieces use **900 Pt** (90%) or **850 Pt** (85%) — lower purity means less precious metal and slightly different colour. The [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/) certify loose stones, not metal — metal purity is verified by the hallmark.

### How does platinum compare to palladium?

Palladium is in the platinum group (similar appearance) but costs less. Palladium rings are ~$200–$400 cheaper than platinum equivalents. Palladium is lighter than platinum and slightly less durable under heavy wear. For engagement rings intended for lifetime wear, platinum is the stronger choice.

### Does platinum work with every marquise setting style?

**Yes — 40+ styles available** in platinum including solitaire, six-prong, bezel, halo, three-stone, pavé, vintage, Art Deco, and east-west. The full market scan above covers all available styles. The only limitation is setting variety — white gold has 20+ more style options at the same price points.

